  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A tight machine chatter: a pulse-warped square through a tuned comb filter that ratchets in sixteenths, folded into a harsh bark over a clean sub. Play short notes or runs on F1, G1 and A#1, mono and legato; the comb follows your keys so the metal stays in tune with the sub, and harder hits push the comb resonance. Macros: Chatter deepens the sixteenth-note ratchet; Comb Tone raises and tightens the comb, which darkens the metal; Fold pushes the wave folder; Square Gate adds an eighth-note spectral jump.",
